  "body": "One policy detail before I change the submit path: should slot end abort an in-flight submission, or only prevent starting further retries? A late successful response can still be useful, especially when reconstructing the legacy full block. I lean toward preserving the first attempt\u2019s configured timeout, while allowing at most two retries only within the signed block\u2019s slot and bounding those retries by the remaining budget.\n\nI found no competing PR. Enforcing a shared cancellation deadline will depend on #10526\u2019s signal fix. I won\u2019t change `getHeader` or the post-Gloas builder API.\n",
